\newlabel{tab:correction_comparison}{{1}{3}{Significance counts (out of 12 benchmark$\times $attack conditions) for $\etamax $ and $\keff $ across correction methods. The $\etamax $:$\keff $ dominance ratio increases from 1.4:1 (OLS) to 5:1 (bootstrap) after correcting for panel non-independence, because $\keff $ significance is more severely inflated by panel overlap than $\etamax $}{table.1}{}}
