\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {4}{\ignorespaces $\ensuremath  {K_{\text  {eff}}}$ significance and model fit ($R^2$) under random-fault vs.\ adaptive regimes. Under random faults, panel composition is highly predictive ($R^2\approx 0.70$) and $\ensuremath  {K_{\text  {eff}}}$ is genuinely significant. Under adaptive attacks, predictability collapses ($R^2\approx 0.22$) and $\ensuremath  {K_{\text  {eff}}}$ significance is largely artifactual.}}{5}{table.4}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:bft}{{4}{5}{$\keff $ significance and model fit ($R^2$) under random-fault vs.\ adaptive regimes. Under random faults, panel composition is highly predictive ($R^2\approx 0.70$) and $\keff $ is genuinely significant. Under adaptive attacks, predictability collapses ($R^2\approx 0.22$) and $\keff $ significance is largely artifactual}{table.4}{}}
